e is  going to be ignorant to the situation so  that's given the government something to  feed off of one of the things we know  about rap music is that rappers fashion  characters write and evidence of the of  that is the fact that they often use  other names besides their own not always  but most often  so there's the andre mitchell who is the  individual who is the person but then  there's the person he created the rapper  he created last boy and what happens as  we tend to assume they're one in the  same  deandre is the family man I have two  kids and everything but when when I do  music I build my character to be lads  the boy and that's that that's just  another it's just another image if you  get around me and really understand me  see what's going on you see that it  really is just an image it's not it's  not Hawaiian there's a lot of wordplay  there's a lot of exaggeration there's a  lot of metaphor simile the goal is to  use wordplay often to invert me if you  see a movie or something and it looks so  realistic and bring goosebumps your arms  you really could feel it you know to me  and that's just how I feel that's just  hot trying to make my music feel when  you actually look at the content it's  clear that this is actually drawing on  real-life experiences involving  real-life men who have in fact who had  their lives ended due to gang violence  they don't do it to anybody else's music  just only hip-hop music they don't do it  to rock n roll they don't do it the  country reggae  kuroh headed back  but I shot a man in Reno just to watch  him  well one Johnny Cash is dead but it even  Johnny Cash were alive as far as I know  no one ever suspected him of shooting  someone in Reno if he had done that and  he was charged with that then I think it  might be a different story  I hesitate to go into the motives as to  why it's used but I think that the  effect it has on jurors on ordinary  people without exposure to hip-hop  perpetuates certain myths and  ster